---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import ClassroomHome from "../../components/clubhouse/ClassroomHome";

export const prerender = true;

export const title = "MTX 101 Classroom";
export const navCategory = "clubhouse";
---

<Layout title="MTX 101 Classroom - Matrix Hub">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <p class="mb-2 text-sm text-green-300/80">
      <a href="/clubhouse" class="hover:text-green-300">← The Clubhouse</a>
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4 text-green-400">
      🎓 The MTX 101 Classroom
    </h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-4">
      The MTX 101 series, as slide decks you move through at your own pace —
      arrow keys, on-screen arrows, or swipe. Each lesson ends with two
      check-yourself questions.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mb-6">
      The lessons teach what MTX is, how to check everything yourself, and
      how to stay safe. They are adapted from the approved MTX 101 education
      series, and every fact in them is checked against the public proof
      pack and the <a href="/security" class="text-green-300 underline">/security</a> page.
    </p>

    <div
      class="bg-green-900/40 border-2 border-green-500 rounded-lg p-4 mb-8 text-green-100"
    >
      <strong>Plainly stated:</strong> this is education, not financial
      advice. MTX is a utility token for this website; nothing here talks
      about value going up or down, because that is not what the token is
      for. Your lesson progress is stored only in this browser, on this
      device — no account, nothing sent anywhere — and it will feed your
      Clubhouse Passport.
    </div>

    <ClassroomHome client:only="react" />

    <div class="mt-12 bg-gray-800 border border-gray-600 rounded-lg p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-400 mb-3">
        The syllabus — complete
      </h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
        All thirteen lessons are live above — the full MTX 101 series, from
        what MTX is to the honest gaps in the final lesson. There is no
        "coming soon" list: a new topic joins this classroom only when
        there is verified material to teach, and it will be announced here
        when there is.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-4 text-sm">
        The hands-on companion to these lessons is{' '}
        <a href="/proving-ground" class="text-green-300 underline">the Proving Ground</a> —
        practice the address check, the mint, and contract verification by doing them.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 bg-gray-800 border border-gray-600 rounded-lg p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-400 mb-3">Built from the commons</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300">
        The decks run on <strong class="text-gray-100">reveal.js</strong> (MIT
        Licence), with a built-in fallback slider if it cannot start.
        Lesson-completion celebrations use the vendored{' '}
        <strong class="text-gray-100">canvas-confetti</strong> (ISC Licence).
        Lesson copy is adapted from Anya Kowalski's MTX 101 education series;
        facts are claim-checked against the 2026-11-12 public proof pack.
        Nothing in this room phones home.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
